{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0da987b323ed937fe2f0670d9e5ee6a841894784362689ee0aadc515ef4cfb5f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README gives kimi mcp add examples for HTTP, HTTP with OAuth, and stdio servers, and documents ad-hoc connections through the --mcp-config-file option."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2de7cbb8e74f3dfc5559ed151ee9a01149bc2bf99c6e6455bf0f64cb702afa66"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A prominent README notice states Kimi CLI is evolving into Kimi Code CLI from the same team, that installing Kimi Code CLI automatically migrates existing configuration and sessions, and that this project will be gradually wound down while its docs and existing installs remain available."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7b7d9a373b763ae37df9b95f3b6e05a53c9b51887025ab28b1cd617f6215b663"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation states Kimi CLI supports the Agent Client Protocol out of the box, so it can run as an ACP agent server for ACP-compatible editors such as Zed or JetBrains after completing login in the terminal first."},{"claim_ids":["clm_87f753f389ecfe88ecf9f94ee590917c1f1e7c69f42ba36a84c8595eb39f5d62"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation describes a shell command mode toggled with Ctrl-X that runs shell commands without leaving Kimi CLI, noting built-in shell commands like cd are not yet supported in that mode."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a45d0534e9a3a87cacd4f8350c8c928574e53c726cce9382b176a911c376334a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README describes Kimi CLI as a terminal AI agent that helps complete software development tasks and terminal operations: it reads and edits code, executes shell commands, searches and fetches web pages, and autonomously plans and adjusts actions during execution."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b999aa78f8a734d066282e275a78dd73cd1a5960e0cf889701d9932128f564e6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: Documented development commands include make format, make check for linting and type checking, make test, and separate make test-kimi-cli, make test-kosong, and make test-pykaos targets for each component."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0da987b323ed937fe2f0670d9e5ee6a841894784362689ee0aadc515ef4cfb5f","clm_2de7cbb8e74f3dfc5559ed151ee9a01149bc2bf99c6e6455bf0f64cb702afa66","clm_7b7d9a373b763ae37df9b95f3b6e05a53c9b51887025ab28b1cd617f6215b663","clm_87f753f389ecfe88ecf9f94ee590917c1f1e7c69f42ba36a84c8595eb39f5d62","clm_a45d0534e9a3a87cacd4f8350c8c928574e53c726cce9382b176a911c376334a","clm_b999aa78f8a734d066282e275a78dd73cd1a5960e0cf889701d9932128f564e6"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:48:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_26e3f4a8703e4983bf19fad5e0382d40","id":"pg_5779ca4d5d68504e93ef34f767825666","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/moonshotai-kimi-cli-readme-md-86f136422a0a-34f767825666.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_ceb0112111655e848d680a209a8a73ff"],"title":"MoonshotAI/kimi-cli/README.md @ 86f136422a0a","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:48:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_26e3f4a8703e4983bf19fad5e0382d40"}
